19:27:10 run E29 20260918-192710: What makes a wild pack approach and attack a fortress? v6.1's safety question: an irruption that cannot be aimed is a hazard rather than a feature. The agitated arm sets flags4.agitated_wilderness_creature on every wild land unit and RE-APPLIES IT AT EVERY SAMPLE; the control leaves them alone. The re-application is not a convenience — CTRL carries ZERO wild land units at t0 in run after run (T7b and E32 both sampled land=0 on their first pass), so a one-shot flag at t0 flags nothing at all and the arm becomes its own control. It also matches how v6.1 would really work: an irruption module would hold the flag as a job, the way the ecology switch holds relations. Each sample counts BEFORE re-flagging, so decay between samples is still measured. Sampled every 3,000 ticks for wild units within fifteen tiles of the dwarves' centroid, how many carry the flag, and what combat is logged. A season on CTRL, two replicates each. The fort may well die in the agitated arm — that is a result.
